@startuml 12-sequence-retour
' UML sequence diagram: a Retour, with the mandatory client signature (US-070 to US-075).
!include style.iuml
hide footbox
autonumber "<b>0."

actor "Staff" as staff
actor "Client" as client
participant "App\n(iPhone)" as app
participant "Data API +\nPostgreSQL" as db
participant "Storage" as st

== Open the rental · US-070 ==
staff -> app : « Retour », choose the active rental
app -> db : load the contract as last amended, departure data, open damage
app -> st : signed links for the reference photos (≤ 5 min)

== Check-in · US-071 to US-073 ==
staff -> app : return time, km in, fuel in
app -> app : km driven, extra km
alt new damage
  loop each new damage
    staff -> app : at least one photo + a comment
    app -> st : upload the photos (insert-only)
    app -> db : save as open damage, linked to this Retour
  end
else nothing new
  staff -> app : « RAS »
end
opt dashboard photo (optional)
  staff -> app : photo of km and fuel
  app -> st : upload (insert-only)
end
staff -> app : final pricing lines, typed by hand
app -> db : Retour saved as it is typed (in progress)

== Signature, mandatory · US-074 ==
alt client present
  app -> client : recap: km, fuel, new damage or RAS, final amounts
  client -> app : signs once on the pad
  app -> st : upload the signature image first
  app -> db : rpc complete_return(contract, signature, idempotency key)
  activate db #F6EFDC
  db -> db : one transaction:\nreturn inspection completed · final amounts\nsignature evidence · car km and fuel\ncontract closed · car available · audit
  db --> app : closed
  deactivate db
  staff -> app : choose Français or English (US-075)
  app -> app : final PDF: Départ and Retour,\nboth signatures bottom right of every page
  app -> st : upload the PDF
  app -> db : record the PDF (stage final)
  app -> staff : iOS share sheet
else client absent
  app -> staff : « Retour en attente de signature »
  note right of app : The contract stays active and the car « En cours ».\nThe company contacts the client (B-08), and the\nRetour is finished when the client signs.
end
@enduml
